    "after_contains": "The physical buffer layout is an implementation decision",
    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/gpu-byte-address.svg\" alt=\"A contiguous instance buffer is expanded into a 64-byte teaching record with three transform rows and tint; arithmetic obtains address 0x10F0 for instance 3 tint.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"650\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Add a hypothetical fourth pot to the captured three-pot group, then follow its highlighted instance record, then its yellow final field. A logical instance ID becomes an address only after applying the stride and field offset. The CPU packing code and GPU decoding code must share that contract. This 64-byte example is deliberately invented for arithmetic clarity; Unreal GPU Scene has its own versioned layouts and additional tables.</figcaption></figure>"
