    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/deformation-bounds.svg\" alt=\"A schematic room mannequin outside the camera region extends a hand into it. A stale red dashed bound excludes the hand and fails the visibility test; a larger green current-pose bound intersects the region.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"620\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>In this schematic closeup of the same room mannequin, the red dashed rest bound lies entirely left of the view boundary, so culling it is internally consistent but visually wrong: the hand has moved into the image. The current green bound includes the hand and survives. A larger correct bound may cost more culling work; a smaller incorrect bound loses visible geometry.</figcaption></figure>"
