    "after_contains": "Material instances reuse a parent material",
    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/material-response.svg\" alt=\"Four real Unreal captures of the same indoor room separate base color, roughness and metallic from the final lit result.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"870\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Track the short matte block at screen left and the tall glossy block at screen right through all four frames. Roughness and metallic are material inputs; neither is an image of illumination. The lit frame adds direct and indirect illumination, visibility and display processing. The blocks differ in base color, roughness and metallic, so their appearance is not evidence for a roughness-only causal comparison. These panels embed unchanged images from the <a href=\"assets/unreal-lab/capture-manifest.json\">native Unreal capture run</a>.</figcaption></figure>"
